{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"8f3445ef48ef48b5","name":"card_event_bocage_warfare","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BloodIron/events/card_event_bocage_warfare","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BOCAGE WARFARE","text":"Give a unit in your support line: \"Gets +2+2 when it moves into the frontline.\"","flavorText":"Bocage warfare refers to the intense fighting that took place in the dense hedgerow countryside of Normandy, France, during WWII. The “Battle of the Hedgerows” occurred in June and July 1944, with extremely deadly fighting raging for three weeks. This challenging bocage landscape, characterized by small fields, high hedges, and muddy lanes, created natural defenses for the German army and slowed down the Allied progression. The hedgerows provided excellent cover for German infantry, tanks, and artillery, allowing them to set up ambushes and resist the Allies push inland. American troops had to adapt quickly, developing new tactics and modifying equipment to navigate and fight in the bocage. For instance, tanks were fitted with improvised \"hedge cutters\", known as Rhino attachments, to break through the thick hedgerows. Allied infantry also adopted close-quarters combat tactics to clear fortified positions hidden within the terrain. Despite high casualties and slow progress, these adaptations allowed the Allies to eventually break through the German defenses and continue their advance in Normandy.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_bocage_warfare","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_bocage_warfare_title","SourceString":"BOCAGE WARFARE","LocalizedString":"BOCAGE WARFARE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_bocage_warfare_text","SourceString":"Give a unit in your support line: \"Gets +2+2 when it moves into the 