 equipment to navigate and fight in the bocage. For instance, tanks were fitted with improvised \"hedge cutters\", known as Rhino attachments, to break through the thick hedgerows. Allied infantry also adopted close-quarters combat tactics to clear fortified positions hidden within the terrain. Despite high casualties and slow progress, these adaptations allowed the Allies to eventually break through the German defenses and continue their advance in Normandy."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardMoveToFrontline"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/Winter_2024/t_bocage_warfare.t_bocage_warfare","SubPathString":""},"artist":"US WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/BOCAGE_WARFARE.BOCAGE_WARFARE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":407.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_bocage_warfare_photo","SourceString":"US forces fighting in the French bocage, July 1944. ","LocalizedString":"US forces fighting in the French bocage, July 1944. "},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"isAttackBuff":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"tempCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_bocage_warfare_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event"